### Goal Model for Multi-Robot Resource Collection and Delivery Mission

#### Goals

| Name | Text | Runtime | Goal Type | Relation | Justification |
|------|------|---------|-----------|----------|---------------|
| G1 | Execute Resource Collection and Delivery Mission | - | Achieve | - | Ensures the overall mission success. |
| G2 | Collect Required Resources | - | Perform | AND | Sequential after G1. |
| G3 | Deliver Collected Resources | - | Perform | AND | Sequential after G2. |
| G4 | Request Resources from Storage A | - | Perform | OR | Parallel collection from different storages. |
| G5 | Request Resources from Storage B | - | Perform | OR | Parallel collection from different storages. |
| G6 | Deliver Resources to Destination A | - | Perform | OR | Parallel deliveries to different locations. |
| G7 | Deliver Resources to Destination B | - | Perform | OR | Parallel deliveries to different locations. |

#### Tasks

| Name | Text | Relation | Location | Number of Robots | Justification |
|------|------|----------|----------|-------------------|---------------|
| AT1 | Request Resources from Storage A | OR | Storage A | 1 | Single robot per storage for parallel collection. |
| AT2 | Request Resources from Storage B | OR | Storage B | 1 | Single robot per storage for parallel collection. |
| AT3 | Deliver Resources to Destination A | OR | Destination A | 1 | Single robot per destination for parallel delivery. |
| AT4 | Deliver Resources to Destination B | OR | Destination B | 1 | Single robot per destination for parallel delivery. |

### Logical Relationships

- **G1 -> G2, G3 [AND]**
  - Justification: Collection must precede delivery.

- **G2 -> G4, G5 [OR]**
  - Justification: Multiple robots can collect from different storages in parallel.

- **G2 -> AT1, AT2 [AND]**
  - Justification: All storages must be addressed for complete collection.

- **G3 -> G6, G7 [OR]**
  - Justification: Multiple robots can deliver to different destinations in parallel.

- **G3 -> AT3, AT4 [AND]**
  - Justification: All deliveries must be completed for mission success.

### Summary

The goal model is structured to ensure efficient resource collection and delivery through parallel execution of tasks, with fallback mechanisms for battery issues. Each goal is decomposed into tasks that can be executed by robots in parallel, ensuring the mission is completed efficiently.
